From a9d3d22cc5f3227a93b56857ca061e5d99eba8c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Kerello <christophe.kerello@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 11:02:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 453/572] fix(st-nvmem): Fix an overflow in
 stm32_tamp_nvram_read function

Fix an overflow issue in stm32_tamp_nvram_read function when we read
a single byte.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git a3c0318642215c6e29efec84733ef853ef874b68 fix(st-nvmem): Fix an overflow in stm32_tamp_nvram_read function]
Change-Id: I347261046e9a931a55de4128cb19a2db79f58417
Signed-off-by: Christophe Kerello <christophe.kerello@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/548958
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Christophe KERELLO <christophe.kerello@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Christophe KERELLO <christophe.kerello@st.com>
---
 drivers/st/nvmem/stm32mp_tamp_nvram_core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/st/nvmem/stm32mp_tamp_nvram_core.c b/drivers/st/nvmem/stm32mp_tamp_nvram_core.c
index e12d1d2490..de6a58c2e9 100644
--- a/drivers/st/nvmem/stm32mp_tamp_nvram_core.c
+++ b/drivers/st/nvmem/stm32mp_tamp_nvram_core.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ stm32_tamp_nvram_read(struct stm32_tamp_nvram_drv_data *drv_data, size_t offset,
 				ERROR("BKPreg %zu is not allowed to be read\n", reg_idx);
 				byte = 0;
 			}
-			buf_u8[i] = byte;
+			buf_u8[i - offset] = byte;
 			i++;
 		}
 	}
-- 
